S("00oV6DJkK3E","Binaural Beats Explained: Build One in Your DAW with Binaura",
 "binaural-rate-ramp-eased-symmetric-offset-gearbox-dwell-shift-band-steps-harmonic-same-gap-isochronic-blend",
 "Rate-ramp brainwave layer: a binaural pair centred on a fixed carrier (e.g. 200 Hz) with the beat split symmetrically (carrier minus beat/2 left, plus beat/2 right) and the beat rate moved over time, either as one eased (slow-fast-slow) ramp from a start to a target rate (e.g. 6 -> 1.5 Hz over minutes) or as a 'gearbox' of band steps (16 -> 10 -> 6 -> 2 Hz) that dwell for minutes and shift over ~1-1.5 min, with an optional return trip; a harmonic second pair (fifth/octave/12th) keeping the same gap, an isochronic amplitude pulse at the same rate blended in for speakers, and a brown-noise bed",
 "Build the slow-ramp-between-pulse-rates layer the brainwave cluster was missing. Delta vs brainwave-binaural-isochronic-layers (fixed-rate binaural, isochronic, monaural/tremolo variants): the beat rate is automated over time while the carrier centre stays fixed, with an eased single ramp or a stepped dwell/shift schedule, plus same-gap harmonic doubling.",
 ["Two sine oscillators (or one per channel) with automatable frequency, hard-panned L/R","An amplitude LFO/tremolo or gate for the isochronic blend","A brown-noise source","Headphones for checking the binaural part"],
 [("carrier_hz","number","Centre pitch, 20-1000 Hz; e.g. 200, or an octave above the drone root (220 over an A2 drone)",True),("start_beat_hz","number","Starting beat rate, e.g. 6 or 16",True),("target_beat_hz","number","Target beat rate, e.g. 1.5 or 2",True),("ramp_minutes","number","Ramp length (up to ~60 min); or dwell/shift times for gearbox mode",True)],
 [("brainwave_layer","audio","Stereo binaural (+ optional isochronic) layer whose beat rate ramps or steps while pitch centre stays fixed"),("rate_schedule","text","Time -> beat-rate table used for the automation")],
 ["Move the beat, not the pitch: both ears move toward each other by the same amount (left = carrier - beat/2, right = carrier + beat/2), so the perceived centre pitch never changes.","Ramps are eased (leave slowly, faster in the middle, settle gently on the target); no jumps or random rate changes.","Binaural beats need headphones; if the track must work on speakers, blend in an isochronic pulse at the same rate (amplitude dip 0.6 = partial, 1.0 = to silence), which lives in each channel's signal.","Keep the carrier above the bass register and in a free part of the mix; to make it fuller add a harmonic pair (fifth = 1.5x, octave = 2x, 12th = 3x carrier) with the same gap rather than turning the tone up.","Tone level around -14 dBFS peak, brown noise bed around -26 dB; fade the layer in over ~10 s.","The plugin's 'phi ladder' and 'intention' carrier presets are vendor-specific/unverified claims and are omitted.","Not medical advice; entrainment effects are not guaranteed.",ABL,"Portable module mapping: two sines with frequency automation (or one sine through a stereo frequency shifter), an LFO-driven VCA for isochronic, a noise generator; works in any DAW or Web Audio (OscillatorNode.frequency.setTargetAtTime / linearRampToValueAtTime)."],
 [("Pick the carrier: e.g. 200 Hz, or an octave above the bed's drone root (A2 drone -> 220 Hz carrier) so it stays above the bass.","Sine osc x2","Carrier chosen with room in the mix"),
  ("Set the start beat: left sine = carrier - beat/2, right sine = carrier + beat/2 (6 Hz at 200 -> 197 L / 203 R); hard-pan each.","Panned sines","On headphones a 6 Hz pulse heard though neither channel pulses"),
  ("Classic ramp: draw automation on both oscillators so the gap moves from the start to the target rate (e.g. 6 -> 1.5 Hz) over the ramp time, with an S-shaped (eased) curve; both frequencies move symmetrically.","Frequency automation","Pulse slows smoothly; centre pitch steady"),
  ("Gearbox alternative: write a schedule of band steps without skipping a band (e.g. 16 beta -> 10 alpha -> 6 theta -> 2 delta Hz), hold each for a dwell (default ~4 min; 30 s for previews) and shift between them over a gear-shift time (~1.5 min; 15 s for previews).","Stepped automation","Audible holds and smooth gear changes"),
  ("Decide the ending: return trip (back up 2 -> 6 -> 10 -> 16), hold the last band and fade out after one dwell, or hold the final rate to the end.","Automation","Defined session ending"),
  ("Optional harmonic: add a second pair at octave (397/403 for 200 Hz + 6), fifth (1.5x) or 12th (3x) of the carrier with the same gap, both pairs following the same rate automation.","Second sine pair","Fuller tone, same beat"),
  ("Optional isochronic blend: tremolo/VCA on the tones at the current beat rate (follows the same automation), depth ~0.6 for a partial dip or 1.0 to silence.","LFO -> VCA","Pulse remains audible on speakers"),
  ("Add a brown-noise bed (~-26 dB) and fade the whole layer in over ~10 s; set tone peak ~-14 dBFS; place under the pad/drone.","Noise + gain","Warm bed, tone not crowding the low end")],
 ["At any time t, (right Hz - left Hz) equals the scheduled beat rate and (left + right)/2 equals the carrier.","Rate automation curve has no steps outside the gearbox shifts and no random segments.","Summed to mono the binaural part has no level pulsing; with isochronic on, a pulse is still audible on speakers."],
 ["brainwave","binaural","isochronic","rate-ramp","automation","entrainment","sine","meditation"])

S("rEXT0z75IyQ","Hybrid Film Scoring: Blending Orchestral and Granular Textures with Samplers",
 "orchestral-ostinato-bounce-to-sampler-octave-down-half-speed-pulse-stack-drive-filter-fader-console-shimmer-granular-position-modwheel-scan-remarry-live-orchestra",
 "Hybrid orchestral sound design: bounce a string ostinato (or piano loop) to audio, load it into a sampler/granular synth, play it one and two octaves down so it repitches to half and quarter speed and stack the octaves into a slow pulse; add a filtered arpeggiated bass and a filtered simple analog lead; process with drive -> a fader-mapped morphing filter -> console/compressor -> big shimmer reverb; then switch the same sample to granular with a held position scanned by the mod wheel (or a slow synced LFO), optionally FM/ring-mod or wave-shape it; finally blend the processed layer back under the real orchestral parts (e.g. horns with heavy reverb)",
 "Turn orchestral library material into otherworldly hybrid-score textures. Delta vs granular cluster (sampler loop chord pad, keygroup, freeze stacks) and synth-strings cluster: the source is a composed orchestral ostinato, repitched by octaves into a tempo-related pulse, then remarried with the live orchestral parts.",
 ["An orchestral ostinato or piano loop you wrote/rendered (bounced to audio, 16-bit WAV is safest for older samplers)","A sampler with repitch playback and a granular mode (any DAW sampler, a hybrid synth)","Distortion, a sweepable filter, a channel compressor, a large/shimmer reverb"],
 [("ostinato","audio","Bounced string ostinato or piano loop in the cue's key",True),("cue_tempo","number","Cue tempo",True),("orchestral_parts","midi","Real orchestral lines to keep (e.g. horns, strings)",False)],
 [("hybrid_pulse","audio","Octave-stacked, processed ostinato pulse"),("granular_pad","audio","Position-scanned evolving pad from the same sample"),("hybrid_cue","arrangement","Processed layers blended under real orchestral parts")],
 ["Steady pitch: repitch only by whole octaves (half/quarter speed) so the layers stay in key; use the granular 'position' mode (held/scanned position), not random 'speed' grain spray; skip the stepped pitch-modulating pulse effect from the source (Matt's preference).","Filter sweeps and position scans are slow, hand-drawn or synced; no rapid clicking gates.","Only process material you composed/rendered yourself; do not redistribute library loops or presets.",EARLY,ABL,"Portable module mapping: sampler (repitch, no time-lock) -> drive -> morph/multimode filter on a macro -> console-style saturation + compressor -> shimmer reverb; granular = sample buffer with grain position on mod wheel/LFO; FM/ring mod and waveshaper as optional colour."],
 [("Write or render a string ostinato (or piano loop) and bounce it to an audio file.","Bounce","Source sample in the cue key"),
  ("Load it into a sampler with repitch (non time-locked) playback; play the root, then one octave down (half speed) and two octaves down (quarter speed); hold them together for a layered pulse.","Sampler","Slow, tempo-related pulse that still sounds orchestral"),
  ("Add a simple arpeggiated bass, filtered so it isn't in your face, and a simple analog-style lead filtered down further.","Synth + low-pass","Three layers moving at different paces"),
  ("Insert drive/distortion on the sample layer (play the low octave to hear it turn otherworldly), not overdone.","Distortion","Grit and harmonics"),
  ("Add a morphing/multimode filter and map its cutoff to a fader or macro; ride it darker to build tension.","Filter + macro","Radical tone change from one control"),
  ("Add a console-style channel strip/compressor after the filter, then a large shimmer-type reverb coloured to taste.","Saturation/comp + reverb","Pad-like, sound-designed wash"),
  ("Switch the same sample to granular in position mode; map grain position to the mod wheel (or a slow tempo-synced LFO) and scan through the sample while chords are held; optionally add FM, ring mod or waveshaper for an alien colour.","Granular position + mod wheel","Evolving, morphing pad that no longer reads as strings"),
  ("Optionally load a piano loop into a granular engine, low-pass it, play two octaves down and let the scan run forward or backward.","Granular + LP","Unrecognisable tension texture"),
  ("Blend back: keep some real orchestral parts (e.g. horns, strings), add heavy reverb to them, and marry them with the processed layers in the cue.","Mix","Modern hybrid score texture")],
 ["Octave-stacked layers stay in the cue's key (only +/-12/24 semitone repitch).","Granular pad has no random pitch spray; scanning is smooth.","Processed layer and real orchestra are both audible in the final blend."],
 ["orchestral","hybrid","sampler","granular","film-score","resampling","texture","tension"])

S("X2xijc3S8cc","How to create AMAZING Pads & Drones (for any genre) - Sound Design Tutorial",
 "pad-vs-drone-roles-aux-verb-as-cohesion-layer-ensemble-split-octave-displace-tuned-field-drone-octave-copy-top-down-mix-drone-last",
 "Pad and drone layering from synth to mix: decide the role (pad follows chords, drone holds one note as a bed); a slow-attack/release poly saw pad with a subtle slow cutoff LFO, octave-down sub, unison and a different second wavetable; reverb on an aux treated as its own layer (low-cut, optional octave-up crystallizing effect and a slow LFO on overdrive mix) for timbral cohesion; a ping-pong looped sampler pad layered by splitting each chord (bottom two notes to one layer, top two to the other) and displacing octaves (+2 / -1); a drone from a tonal slice of a field recording, warped, looped, tuned to key, low-cut and reverbed, doubled two octaves down; then a top-down mix where the pad is EQ'd around bass and vocal with light sidechain and the drone goes in last at barely audible level",
 "Build and place an evolving pad + drone bed that glues a track. Delta vs pad/wavetable/supersaw and harmony clusters: the aux reverb is treated as a layer for timbral cohesion, chord tones are split between layers with octave displacement to free frequency space, a key-tuned field-recording drone is doubled two octaves down, and the mix order puts the drone in last, just audible.",
 ["A poly wavetable/VA synth with LFOs and unison","A sampler with ping-pong loop + crossfade","An aux reverb return, EQ, overdrive, sidechain compressor","A field recording with a tonal section"],
 [("chords","midi","Chord progression, e.g. 4-note chords",True),("key","string","Track key for drone tuning",True),("field_recording","audio","Atmosphere with a sustained pitched part",False)],
 [("pad_group","audio","Two complementary pad layers grouped with shared EQ/comp/filter automation"),("drone","audio","Tuned field-recording drone plus octave-down double"),("mix_notes","text","EQ cuts around bass/vocal, sidechain amount, drone level")],
 ["Steady pitch: no pan/position LFO flutter on pitch and no wow-and-flutter tape emulation on the melodic pad (the source's tape wow is dropped); LFOs only on cutoff, mix and pan, at slow rates with small depth (Matt's preference).","Layers must complement, not double: use a different waveform for the second oscillator/layer.","Set enough voices for overlapping releases (e.g. 8 voices for two overlapping 4-note chords).","Octave-shift arithmetic for the drone: if tuned at +4 semitones, two octaves down is -20.",EARLY,ABL,"Portable module mapping: saw + sub + unison -> LP with slow LFO; aux reverb -> EQ low cut -> pitch-shift/octave-up granular -> overdrive with LFO on mix; sampler ping-pong loop with crossfade; audio warp/transpose for drone tuning."],
 [("Decide the role: pad (follows the chord progression) or drone (one held note as an emotional bed).","Planning","Role written down"),
  ("Pad: poly saw, add attack and release so chords blend in and out; low-pass with a small, slow LFO on cutoff; add an octave-down sub and unison for thickness.","Synth amp env + LFO","Smoothly fading, gently evolving pad"),
  ("Add a second oscillator with a different waveform, a little unison, a slow pan LFO and an optional slow wavetable-position LFO at low depth; add chorus/dimension and an optional flanger-type filter with slow LFO on cutoff and mix.","Osc B + LFOs","Complementary layer, not mud"),
  ("Create an aux return with a 100% wet reverb, low-cut its EQ, optionally add an octave-up crystallizing pitch effect and an overdrive whose mix is moved by a slow, shallow LFO; send the pad to it. Treat this return as a layer.","Aux reverb chain","Wide, cohesive space from the same source"),
  ("Sampler pad layer: a one-note sample (pitched on C) in ping-pong loop mode with crossfade, attack and release added, enough voices; copy the chords to it.","Sampler","Second pad layer in tune"),
  ("Split each chord: synth layer keeps the bottom two notes, sampler layer the top two; move the top pair up two octaves and the bottom pair down one; send the sampler layer to the same aux.","MIDI edit","Ensemble chord with frequency space between layers"),
  ("Group the pad layers; apply shared EQ, light compression and a slowly opening filter automation.","Group bus","Pads behave as one instrument"),
  ("Drone: find a section of a field recording with a single pitch, loop and warp it, transpose to the track key, low-cut, add reverb on the channel; duplicate and drop two octaves.","Audio warp + EQ + reverb","Textural drone in key"),
  ("Top-down mix: with the main elements balanced, bring the pad in loud to hear clashes, cut its low end where the bass lives and its top where the vocal lives, add light kick sidechain; bring the drone in last until just audible, with less sidechain than the pad.","EQ + sidechain","Pad sits around bass/vocal; drone glues, noticed mainly when muted")],
 ["Synth and sampler layers never play the same chord tones in the same octave.","Muting the drone removes some high energy/glue but no melodic element.","Pad EQ shows a low cut below the bass's main region."],
 ["pad","drone","layering","reverb","aux","field-recording","mix","sidechain","ensemble-chord"])
